<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<title>Notifications — HeartCode Admin</title>
</head>
<body data-page="notifications">
<div class="admin-shell">
  <%- include('../partials/nav', { activePage: 'notifications' }) %>
  <main class="admin-main">
    <h1 class="mb-2 font-display text-2xl uppercase tracking-wide text-hc-ink">Notifications</h1>
    <p class="mb-6 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-500">
      Get notified the moment a sale completes and a site deploys — across up to 3 email addresses, one webhook, and one Gotify server, all at once. Each channel fires independently: one being down or misconfigured never blocks the others, and never affects the deployment itself. Test a channel before relying on it.
    </p>

    <div class="admin-card max-w-xl">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-hc-ink">Add channel</h2>
      <form id="addChannelForm">
        <label class="admin-label" for="channelType">Channel type</label>
        <select class="admin-select" id="channelType">
          <option value="email">Email (up to 3)</option>
          <option value="webhook">Webhook (1)</option>
          <option value="gotify">Gotify (1)</option>
        </select>

        <label class="admin-label" for="channelLabel">Label</label>
        <input class="admin-input" type="text" id="channelLabel" required placeholder="e.g. My phone">

        <div data-fields="email">
          <label class="admin-label" for="emailAddress">Email address</label>
          <input class="admin-input" type="email" id="emailAddress" placeholder="you@example.com">
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">Sent through whichever email provider is currently active on the Email Providers page.</p>
        </div>

        <div data-fields="webhook">
          <label class="admin-label" for="webhookUrl">Webhook URL</label>
          <input class="admin-input" type="url" id="webhookUrl" placeholder="https://example.com/hooks/heartcode">
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-500">Receives a POST with JSON: <code>{ event, websiteType, clientEmail, siteUrl, amount, currency, deployedAt }</code>. Include any auth token directly in the URL's query string if the endpoint needs one.</p>
        </div>

        <div data-fields="gotify">
          <label class="admin-label" for="gotifyServerUrl">Gotify server URL</label>
          <input class="admin-input" type="url" id="gotifyServerUrl" placeholder="https://gotify.example.com">
          <label class="admin-label" for="gotifyToken">Application token</label>
          <input class="admin-input" type="password" id="gotifyToken" placeholder="From Gotify → Apps → your app's token">
        </div>

        <p id="addChannelError" class="admin-msg admin-msg-error" style="display:none;"></p>
        <button type="submit" class="admin-btn mt-3">Add channel</button>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div id="channelsList" class="mt-6 space-y-4"></div>
  </main>
</div>
</body>
</html>
